 "title": "Backoff and jitter",
 "sources": [
  "AWS Architecture Blog, 'Exponential Backoff And Jitter' (official, fetched 2026-11-17): without jitter, backed-off clients still produce clusters of calls; jitter is trying to improve the performance of a system by adding randomness; the randomness spreads the retry spikes into an approximately constant rate of calls. Not claimed: which jitter variant is best, because the article's comparison is nuanced. https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/architecture/exponential-backoff-and-jitter/",
  "Illustration, not a quoted case: the thousand clients and the 1, 2, 4, 8 second waits are example numbers, labelled on screen. Capping retries is engineering advice."
 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "A thousand clients lose their connection to your server, and all of them retry at the same moment.",
   "caps": "*1000 CLIENTS | ALL RETRY *TOGETHER"
  },
  {
   "text": "The server just came back, and the retry wave knocks it right over again.",
   "caps": "SERVER *RECOVERS | RETRY WAVE *KNOCKS IT OVER"
  },
  {
   "text": "Exponential backoff helps: each retry waits twice as long as the last, so one second, two, four, eight.",
   "caps": "*EXPONENTIAL BACKOFF | *DOUBLE THE WAIT | 1, 2, 4, *8"
  },
  {
   "text": "That spreads the retries out over time, instead of hammering the server every second.",
   "caps": "SPREADS *OVER TIME | NOT EVERY *SECOND"
  },
  {
   "text": "Each client now retries one, two, four, and eight seconds after its own failure.",
   "caps": "*1, 2, 4, 8 | AFTER ITS *OWN FAILURE"
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the catch: if every client started at the same moment, they still retry together, in clusters.",
   "caps": "BUT THERE IS A *CATCH | SAME START | *STILL CLUSTERS"
  },
  {
   "text": "The fix is jitter, which means adding randomness to each wait, and that spreads the spikes into a roughly constant rate.",
   "caps": "*JITTER | ADD *RANDOMNESS | *CONSTANT RATE"
  },
  {
   "text": "So double the wait each time, add randomness, and always cap the number of retries.",
   "caps": "*DOUBLE | *RANDOMIZE | *CAP THE RETRIES"
  }
 ],
